{"description":"Launch a Codex CLI worker with codex exec --json and track its events. workspaceKind controls where it runs: Git work writes only in an isolated git_worktree; read_only_in_place cannot write or use network; scratch writes only under SUPERVISOR_HOME and never lands; in_place_write is only for an explicitly authorized non-Git directory with ownedPaths and acceptance. A non-Git worker may never write the user directory by default. ownedPaths reserves files a landable worker may write; reading is never exclusive. acceptance is the list of shell commands that decide whether the work is done: the supervisor runs them after Codex exits, and workers run the same contract with codex-supervisor-accept. In a Git package project, acceptance using local JavaScript tooling requires workspaceSetup so node_modules and generated prepare files exist before dispatch. The worker's sandbox may write its execution directory, the temp directory and the OS cache directory; a toolchain whose cache lives elsewhere needs writableRoots, a list of existing absolute directories.","execution":{"taskSupport":"forbidden"},"inputSchema":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","properties":{"acceptance":{"anyOf":[{"minLength":1,"type":"string"},{"items":{"anyOf":[{"minLength":1,"type":"string"},{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"baseline":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"failures":{"items":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"kind":{"enum":["failure","error"],"type":"string"},"signature":{"minLength":1,"type":"string"},"test_id":{"minLength":1,"type":"string"}},"required":["test_id","kind","signature"],"type":"object"},"type":"array"},"identity":{"additionalProperties":{"minLength":1,"type":"string"},"properties":{"base_commit":{"minLength":1,"type":"string"}},"required":["base_commit"],"type":"object"},"required":{"items":{"minLength":1,"type":"string"},"type":"array"}},"required":["identity","failures","required"],"type":"object"},"command"